-- cabal.project.stage3.settings - generated by configure from .in template
-- Do not edit this file directly; edit cabal.project.stage3.settings.in instead.
--
-- Stage3 (wasm-cross) settings — hand-crafted, NOT autoconf-substituted via
-- the shared per-package macros. We hard-code `shared: True` to always
-- produce dynamic stage3 wasm libraries (.dyn_hi + .so files) — required
-- for end-user TH-heavy apps (miso, jsaddle, aeson, lens, ...) to compile
-- via the GHC -dynamic-too codepath.
--
-- We deliberately DO NOT set executable-dynamic: True here, unlike stage2.
-- Why: the bindist ships only the wasm-TARGET .so files (under
-- lib/targets/wasm32-unknown-wasi/lib/), not the HOST native dylibs the
-- ghc / ghc-pkg / ghc-iserv binaries would dynamically link against. If
-- the host binaries are dyn-linked, dyld can't find the libHS dylib/so
-- files on the user's machine after extraction:
--
--   dyld: Library not loaded: @rpath/libHSrts-1.0.3-threaded-debug-ghc9.14.dylib
--     Reason: tried '/private/tmp/.../lib/aarch64-apple-darwin/libHSrts-...': no such file
--
-- Static-linking the executables makes them standalone — they only need
-- the wasm-target libs (which ARE shipped) at runtime via the stage3
-- compiler's lookup path. The native libraries are baked into each .o.
--
-- DYNAMIC=0 vs DYNAMIC=1 controls the stage2 (native GHC) dynamic build,
-- but has no effect on stage3 anymore. The wasm bindist always ships
-- shared stage3 libraries.

-- R7 path (i) from lode/phase6-miso-template-draft/REVIEW.md: use `if
-- arch(wasm32) / shared: True` at the project top level — NOT inside
-- a `package *` block. Relies on stable-haskell/cabal's
-- Stage/Toolchain split: BUILD-side packages (deriveConstants,
-- happy-lib, alex, etc.) are evaluated against the native build
-- arch, so `arch(wasm32)` is FALSE for them and `shared: True`
-- doesn't apply → no `-dynamic-too` on the build-side, no need for
-- native base.dyn_hi from stage2.
--
-- HOST-side wasm-target packages (base, ghc-internal, etc.) evaluate
-- `arch(wasm32)` as TRUE, get `shared: True`, and ship both .hi+.dyn_hi
-- and .so. End-user TH-heavy apps (miso, jsaddle, aeson, lens, …)
-- pick these up via cabal's -dynamic-too codepath.
--
-- This depends on the in-tree link fix f92963f43ef ("force rts into
-- wasm32 .so deps even with -no-rts"). Earlier attempts (2026-05-26,
-- before the link fix) failed with GHC-74335 + interface profile tag
-- mismatch; the link fix resolves both.
--
-- DYNAMIC=0 vs DYNAMIC=1 has no effect on stage3 (the conditional
-- is wasm-arch-driven, not configure-flag-driven). It still controls
-- the stage2 native build.

if arch(wasm32)
  package *
    shared: True

constraints:
  rts +dynamic
